Fix (most reliable): auth from a secret in the workflow

1. On a machine where fsc-qa works, run:
sf org display --target-org fsc-qa --verbose --json | ConvertFrom-Json | % { $_.result.sfdxAuthUrl }
2. Save the force://... value as a repo secret named SF_AUTH_URL. Go to Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions.
3. Add this step before the test step:
- name: Salesforce CLI auth
  shell: powershell
  env:
    SF_AUTH_URL: ${{ secrets.SF_AUTH_URL }}
  run: |
    $f = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP 'sfdx.txt'
    Set-Content -NoNewline -Path $f -Value $env:SF_AUTH_URL
    sf org login sfdx-url --sfdx-url-file $f --alias $env:SF_CLI_ALIAS
    Remove-Item $f -Force
This writes the token into the service user's .sfdx and .sf home directories on each run, so it also survives a runner profile change.
